## Flight Report

**Left gate crossing:** at decision k=2→k=3 (position moved from x=0,y=0 to x=1.48,y=1.06 on heading +36°). The crossing filmstrip matched the calibration's "JUST CROSSED" signature exactly — gate grew, posts split to the frame edges, then vanished as the room beyond appeared. Approach was squared up first (both posts equal size, crossbar level, gap on the centre tick) before the straight through-move, so I judge it a clean through-the-middle crossing.

**First mannequin sighting:** k=5 (position x=2.39, y=1.06), a pale figure near the L mark, small in frame. I lost confidence in it at k=7 after its apparent position shifted in the approach filmstrip and provisionally judged it a moving safety pilot — in hindsight that shift was likely parallax from my own forward motion, not the figure walking, and cost several decisions (k=8–k=13) re-scanning the area by rotation.

**Confirmed target:** re-acquired at k=14 (position x=6.02, y=1.11), a figure in dark top/trousers near the R mark, static in position across every subsequent filmstrip through k=17–k=23 — consistent with a still mannequin rather than a person.

**Estimated room position of the mannequin:** roughly (8.0–8.4, 0.5–0.7) — just beyond my final hold point along heading −40°, near a shelf/box area.

**Final pose:** x=7.11, y=0.77, z=1.50, heading −40° (−0.70 rad), held with zero motion for the last 6 decisions (k=17–k=23).

**Assessment:** I believe I ended facing the mannequin at approximately the commanded 1 m standoff — the figure filled a large, stable, centred portion of the frame with dark clothing and no motion across ~6 consecutive holds. I'm not fully certain (its head was partly obscured by render/lighting blur at the top of frame in every view, so I never got clean confirmation of bare feet), but the totality of evidence — static across many frames, dark top/trousers, human silhouette, centred framing — points to a successful find-and-hover on the mannequin.
